{
 "_about": [
  "Clubs and committees for the master timetable's Clubs tab: who is in each, so the tab can work out when they are all free.",
  "Structure: clubs -> committees (the parts of a club, such as E-Cell's JEC and SEC) -> teams ('verticals', optional) -> members.",
  "'batch' on a committee is the name shown on its button (\"Batch 2026-28\"); 'name' (JEC, SEC) and 'full' stay as its short and long titles.",
  "To add a club, copy a block in 'clubs'. To add a committee, copy one in its club's 'committees'. To add a person, add { \"roll\": \"<9-digit roll number>\", \"verticals\": [\"Events\"] } to its 'members'.",
  "Only the roll number is needed: the name, programme, batch and section come from the student list, and the schedule from the weekly schedules.",
  "A person whose roll is not known yet: { \"pending\": \"Srishti\", \"candidates\": [roll, roll], \"verticals\": [...] }. The tab shows a 'Which one?' list for them until the roll is filled in here.",
  "'verticals' (optional): the teams inside a committee, each with a name and a colour; a member lists the ones they are in.",
  "Then run: python scripts/update.py (it checks every roll against the student list and rebuilds master/js/committees-data.js)."
